From deb380384aedd750e77247310bee33834cd54416 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:22:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(motion): Adaptive clears the rotary developed wrap
 level by level, under the load and kink laws

The rotary wrap ladder no longer rewrites Adaptive to Offset rings: each
developed level runs the HSM planner, and every developed arc is chorded
before wrapping, so each world move is posed radially. A seam law
(hsm::Seam, period 2*pi*R_ref per cover) refuses Adaptive by name for a
level whose centre component reaches a cover end short of a full lap;
any planner refusal on the wrap names "the developed level at radius R"
and Offset rings cut that level. Offset rings themselves are unchanged
(digest pinned against main).

Readings (release; r6 wall / r5 neck bar in r7 stock, BN D6, leave 0.5,
stepdown 0.5, Helix r1; law 14.6 % D + 35 % = 19.7 %): radius 6.5 and
6.0 - 22,528 moves, 19.5 % D, 0 breaks past 5 deg; 5.5 - 7,416 moves,
18.8 % D, 0 breaks; 5.0 refused by the planning budget, rings cut it.
No planner overload note (Plunge entry read 76.8 % D in round 1).

Tests (rotary_adaptive): adaptive_plans_the_developed_levels_under_the_load_and_kink_laws
and the_developed_window_reaches_the_planner_and_names_each_refusal
(heavy lane), offset_rings_on_the_wrap_are_the_program_they_always_were
(debug); machining3d::hsm::tests::the_seam_cuts_an_area_at_a_cover_end_short_of_a_lap.
Follow-ups: #54 (D-flat wrap, seam end-to-end), #55 (r6.2 levels, helix
overload, load margin).

Fixes #9

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
