+/// (Its Plunge twin read (5194, 6097177489831100083) both there and on
+/// round 1's patched build.)
+const GOLDEN_RINGS: (usize, u64) = (5263, 2_919_766_036_457_321_567);

From a9b2d8ab625046ece1fa5670bd216dbb4ca404bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:55:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(motion): the rotary Adaptive wrap holds the kink law
 on its posted chords, and names every ring-cut level

Review fixes on PR #57:
- wrap_exit chords each developed XY arc under Adaptive at a 4 deg
  angular cap as well as the sagitta, with 0.01 mm end chords so arc
  junctions gain next to nothing. OffsetRings keeps sagitta-only chords.
- The heavy test pulls the world program back into the developed frame
  and reads its in-cut breaks. Whole bar: sagitta only, 98,525 world
  moves and 12,824 breaks past 5 deg on the planned levels; 4 deg cap,
  160,989 moves and 0 breaks. (A 2.5 deg cap with full-step end chords
  left 14 junction breaks at 138,097 moves.)
- A ring-cut level is read from the program's shape (a cut level with
  no proved arc) and must carry its named note. A named level must post
  no arc. The old check read ring-cut from that same note.
- A hard planner error on the wrap falls back to rings for that level,
  with a named note. The planar ladder still propagates it.
- The proof-tally note says "the developed level at radius R" on the wrap.
- The rings digest hashes on a 1e-6 lattice and is re-pinned. The old
  bitwise digest still matched on the same build.
- The test file has a provenance header.

Refs #9

